@meta{crate: sisho-sdk, dependencies: list(), dependents: list(sisho-cli)}

=[sisho-sdk]

Layer 0: SDK and protocol definitions for `sisho` extensions.

An extension is an independent subprocess on `PATH` named `sisho-<word>`.
This crate provides definitions and utilities for extension developers:

- `info` disclosure protocol (`--sisho-extension-info`).:Metadata
- `jobserver` Jobserver coordination via [`jobserver_gate`].:GNU

==[Module info]

Extension metadata disclosure protocol (`--sisho-extension-info`).

An extension can disclose its name, version, description, and capabilities
by responding to `--sisho-extension-info` with a single JSON object.

===[Structs]

====[struct ExtensionInfo]

Metadata disclosed by an extension when queried with `--sisho-extension-info`.

====[struct Capabilities]

Feature capabilities disclosed by an extension.

===[Constants]

====[const CURRENT_SCHEMA_VERSION]

Current schema version for extension metadata.

====[const EXTENSION_INFO_FLAG]

The standard CLI flag that requests extension metadata.
